'''Todo 360''' was a [[techno-service droid]] owned by [[bounty hunter]] [[Cad Bane]]. During the Clone Wars, Todo served Bane on various missions despite being often overlooked and undervalued by him. Todo participated in the [[Raid on the Jedi Temple|theft]] of a [[holocron]] from the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]], a job that Bane took from [[Darth Sidious]] himself. Although Todo was destroyed when Bane triggered a secret bomb inside of him, the faithful droid was later rebuilt. After, the droid was with Bane for another kidnapping on Coruscant and the subsequent mission to free the gangster [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]] the [[Hutt]] from [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[prison]]. As the [[Jedi]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Quinlan Vos]] attempted to hunt down Bane following the mission, Todo helped Bane battle the two [[Force-sensitive]]s and eventually flee.

Following the end of the Clone Wars, Bane, and thus Todo, continued to find work, including some for the newly formed [[Galactic Empire]]. Todo helped Bane track down the [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] on the planet [[Bracca]], where they eventually captured her. However, Omega would escape their clutches on the planet [[Bora Vio]], where she tricked Todo to initially escape Bane's ship, the ''[[Justifier]]'', and later outfoxed him as she fled. Todo would later accompany Bane to the planet [[Caraad]], where they kidnapped the Force-sensitive child [[Bayrn]] and delivered the [[Tarlafar]] to [[Imperial Station 003]] above Coruscant, receiving a hefty payment.

==History==
===Construction===
Todo 360 was a [[techno-service droid]] created on the [[planet]] [[Vertseth]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> by the [[droid]] manufacturer [[Vertseth Automata]].<ref name="USW" /> Todo 360 was given [[Gender|masculine programming]] and had a height of 0.66 [[meter]]s.<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> Eventually, Todo 360 fell into the hands of [[Cad Bane]], a [[Duros]] [[bounty hunter]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="HH" />

===Sidious's job===
[[File:Bane_fixes_Todo.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Cad Bane secretly plants a bomb in Todo 360.]]
Bane was offered a job to [[Raid on the Jedi Temple|steal]] a [[holocron]] from the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] by [[Darth Sidious]], a [[Sith Lord]] who was secretly manipulating the Republic and [[Separatist Crisis|started]] the [[Clone Wars]] to build his own evil [[Galactic Empire|empire]]. Todo was given a security chip that gave him access to Jedi Temple's security systems, with the permission to disable them. Todo was able to find a weak point in the shields with assistance from the [[Clawdite]] [[Cato Parasitti]]. Todo and Bane then made their way towards the [[Holocron Vault]], encountering little resistance, as Parasitti had given them access via [[Changeling|shapeshifting]] into the deceased [[Jedi Knight]] [[Ord Enisence]]. After losing contact with Cato, Todo was sent to the Temple's [[Jedi Temple communication center|communications center]]. As he entered the communications center, he tried to claim to [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]] that he was a [[maintenance droid]]. In the process, Todo was destroyed not by the [[Jedi]] but by a bomb that Bane had secretly placed inside of him in order to create a distraction as the former succeeded in stealing a holocron.<ref name="HH" />

===The Hutts' job===
[[File:TODO360ConGame-EP.png|thumb|right|200px|Todo 360 attempts to con C-3PO and R2-D2.]]
{{Quote|Thanks for the memories!|Todo 360, to R2-D2 and C-3PO|<ref name="Evil Plans" />}}
After the job at the [[Jedi]] Temple, Todo was rebuilt by the Jedi Knight [[Anakin Skywalker]] in an attempt by the Jedi to learn more about Cad Bane and discover his whereabouts. The plan went wrong and Todo escaped.<ref name="EvilTrivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/evil-plans-trivia-gallery|text="Evil Plans" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> Todo was later reunited with Bane and continued to serve Bane in [[bounty]] hunting. He assisted Bane in kidnapping [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]]'s [[protocol droid]], [[C-3PO]]. He and [[HELIOS-3E]] then kidnapped the [[astromech droid]] [[R2-D2]], C-3PO's companion. After Bane got the [[Galactic Senate|Senate]] [[Imperial Senate Building|Building's]] blueprints for a job to free [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]] the [[Hutt]], Todo and HELIOS-3E dropped off C-3PO and R2-D2 back where they found them.<ref name="HH" />

Bane succeeded in freeing Ziro the Hutt from [[Galactic Republic]] captivity, and<ref name="Hostage Crisis">{{TCW|Hostage Crisis}}</ref> Todo assisted Bane, at the behest of [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder|Gardulla]] and the [[Grand Hutt Council]], in tracking down Ziro in the [[swamp]]s of [[Nal Hutta]]. Both bounty hunters ended up being on the trail of [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Quinlan Vos]], who were also tracking Ziro so they could bring him and Bane into custody. After questioning Ziro's [[Mama|mother]], Todo and Bane went to the planet [[Teth]], only to find Ziro's corpse and [[Hutt Council records|council records]] gone as the Hutt's old flame [[Sy Snootles]] had taken them to Ziro's nephew [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba the Hutt]] for safe keeping. Todo then assisted Bane in escaping the Jedi, attacking Vos and stealing his [[lightsaber]]. Todo attempted to take on Kenobi but was outmatched, but was able to retrieve Bane's hat and escape with him aboard his [[starfighter]], the ''[[Xanadu Blood]]''.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro">{{TCW|Hunt for Ziro}}</ref>

===The Kaminoans' job===
{{Quote|You're in trouble now.|Todo 360, to Hunter and Omega|<ref name="Reunion">{{TBB|Reunion}}</ref>}}
Soon after the fall of the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]], Todo accompanied Bane to [[Bracca]] to capture the [[Gender|female]] [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] by order of [[Kaminoan]] [[Prime Minister]] [[Lama Su]]. The pair encountered clone [[sergeant]] [[Hunter]] protecting their prize, to which Todo stated the clone's dire situation. Todo watched as Bane and Hunter stood off, each with their hands at their sides, ready to fire. Bane acted faster and shot Hunter directly in the chest, causing the sergeant to mistakenly shoot off one of Todo's [[Repulsorlift|booster]] [[Limb|legs]]. Omega tried to fire her energy bow at Bane, but Todo knocked it away with his severed leg. Bane stunned Omega and the two fled the scene, taking Omega hostage.<ref name="Reunion" />

[[File:Todo360FixingHimself-BL.png|left|thumb|240x240px|Todo 360 attempts to fix himself while Omega tries to convince him to let her out.|alt=]]
Following Bane's escape, Todo went to the prison section of Bane's ship, the ''[[Justifier]]'', where Omega demanded Todo let her out. However, Todo refused and told her that Bane doesn't like uncooperative prisoners. After Todo watched Bane speak with Omega, he asked Bane to help him repair his leg, to which Bane ignored him. After Bane went back to the cockpit of the ship, Todo attempted to repair his leg. Omega offered to help Todo if he let her out, to which Todo refused, and said that she was a prisoner and not to be trusted. Eventually, Omega managed to convince Todo to let her out. Honoring what she said, Omega repaired Todo's leg, but then shut down Todo, allowing Omega to search for her [[comm unit]]. Shortly after, Bane came back to the prison section, where he found Omega missing and Todo shut down. Bane reactivated Todo and demanded to know where Omega was, to which Todo replied that she was obviously right beside them, but then realized she had left, leaving him shocked that the girl tricked him.<ref name="Bounty Lost">{{TBB|Bounty Lost}}</ref>

[[File:BoraVioSkirmish.png|thumb|240x240px|Todo is sent flying due to Fennec's detonator, losing the case of credits in the process.]]
After Bane had left to find Omega on the planet they had landed on, Todo called Bane and told him that there was an incoming ship. Once the ship was revealed to be [[Fennec Shand]], who had killed the Kaminoan, [[Taun We]] sent to retrieve Omega, Todo came up behind Shand while her and Bane were in a standoff, and grabbed the case of credits from her. However, as he tried to fly away, a detonator blew up knocking Todo off the edge, who survived with his thrusters, but the credits fell out of the case. After Bane demanded Todo go find Omega, who had just ran away, Todo flew off in search of her. After some time, Todo found Omega and flew into the room she was in but was quickly shot by Shand.

[[File:Todo_360_Hinders_Omega.jpg|left|thumb|240x240px|Todo attempts to stop Omega's escape.]]
Later, as Omega was climbing down a ladder to try to reach a [[Kaminoan flight pod]], Todo flew out of nowhere and they got into a tussle, which ended with Todo being upside down unable to move as Omega ran to the flight pod. Shortly afterwards, Todo caught up and told Omega through the window that she was going to be captured, but then Omega activated flew off in the flight pod, to which Todo yelled that she would regret this. Following this, Todo informed Bane of Omega fleeing in the flight pod and Bane told Todo to ready the ship. However, Omega had been rescued by [[Clone Force 99]] and when Bane arrived, the ship wasn't working because Shand had sabotaged it, leaving them unable to pursue her or the clones.<ref name="Bounty Lost" />

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|I am not a nanny droid!|Todo 360, to Cad Bane|<ref name="Identity Crisis">{{TBB|Identity Crisis}}</ref>}}
[[File:CadBaneTBB-AG.png|thumb|307x307px|Todo worked with Cad Bane during the Imperial Era]]
Todo continued to serve Bane during the rise of the Galactic Empire on several missions tracking force-sensitive children to be used as specimens on the [[Tantiss Base|secret Imperial base]] at [[Mount Tantiss]]. One such mission saw the two act upon a tip from an [[Aqualish]] on the planet [[Caraad]]. Traveling there, Bane and Todo broke into the home of the [[Tarlafar]] [[Ailish]]. Stunning her, Bane ordered Todo to collect a blood sample from her child, [[Bayrn]], to verify his [[Midi-chlorian|M-count]]. Bane then ordered Todo to grab the youngling and keep it quiet. Though he protested, saying he was not a [[nanny droid]], Todo loaded the child into a [[Hover pram|hovering pram]] and gave his toy to silence him. Their target secured, Bane and Todo traveled to [[Imperial Station 003]] above [[Coruscant]] to collect their payment. After Todo verified they had received full payment, the two departed aboard the ''Justifier''.<ref name="Identity Crisis" />

==Personality and traits==
Todo was willing to help Bane capture and obtain his targets, even if they are children, with Todo shown to be willing to mock Bane's prisoners.<ref name="Bounty Lost" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Todo360.jpg|thumb|250px|Concept art of Todo 360|left]]
{{Quote|I do hope that young Boba will be all right.''"<br />"''Don't worry, Todo. He should be fine&hellip; as long as those Sand People ain't hungry.|Todo 360 and Cad Bane|<ref name="Untold CW">{{SWYouTube|7yKM6RExLlI|The Untold Clone Wars Panel &#124; Star Wars Celebration Anaheim}}</ref>}}
Todo 360 was to appear again in the [[The Clone Wars Legacy|bounty hunters arc]] of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' TV series before the show's cancellation. As with other episodes of ''The Clone Wars'', Todo 360 was voiced by [[Seth Green]].<ref name="HH" /><ref name="Untold CW" />

Focused on bounty hunters Cad Bane and [[Boba Fett]] teaming up to retrieve a child kidnapped by [[Tusken Raider]]s, an unfinished reel of the arc shows Todo 360 and the two hunters being ambushed by Tuskens whilst camping on [[Tatooine]]. During the ambush, Boba Fett had himself captured with a [[Homing beacon|tracking device]] linked to Bane in order to locate the Tusken Raider camp, after which Todo hid behind Bane and Fett's [[dewback]] mounts as the assailants were repelled by his master with a [[flamethrower]]. Todo later expressed his concern for Boba Fett's wellbeing, which was dismissed by the more experienced Cad Bane.<ref name="Untold CW" />

